From b4c02ba396fe34f8154f1a275ed40f2d9fb99805 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:12:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: report negotiated IRIS1 encoder plane sizes

IRIS1 queue setup now consults firmware before allocating either queue,
but G_FMT still recomputes sizeimage using only the generic formula.
A client can therefore see a smaller size than the one the same driver
requires for CAPTURE or OUTPUT after REQBUFS.

For an allocated IRIS1 queue, report at least the cached negotiated
minimum. Clear the caller-supplied size before the generic calculation:
G_FMT must report the driver format, not inflate it from arbitrary input.
Do not retain a previous allocation size after buffers are released.

The HFI4 queue-query change is the immediate prerequisite; the Android Q
encoder also copies the firmware requirement into its reported format.
A real-function host test fails on the old G_FMT wrapper and checks both
queue directions with this fix. Verify G_FMT/REQBUFS/QUERYBUF consistency
on hardware. All other Venus platforms keep their existing behavior.

Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index 88f203f15..9c91ed420 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -328,8 +328,19 @@ static int venc_g_fmt(struct file *file, void *fh, struct v4l2_format *f)
 		pixmp->height = inst->out_height;
 	}
 
+	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core))
+		pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = 0;
+
 	venc_try_fmt_common(inst, f);
 
+	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core) &&
+	    vb2_is_busy(v4l2_m2m_get_vq(inst->m2m_ctx, f->type))) {
+		u32 size = V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(f->type) ? inst->input_buf_size :
+							      inst->output_buf_size;
+
+		pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = max(pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage, size);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
